#### Feed-down contributions to \(\Lambda\)

The measured \(\Lambda\) yield includes secondary \(\Lambda\) particles coming from weak decays of heavier hyperons, i.e. \(\Xi^{-}\) and \(\Xi^{0}\), and resonances, \(\sigma*\). In order to disentangle the primary \(\Lambda\) production from the secondary an estimation of this contribution, which is frequently called 'feed-down' is necessary. In the following the method of this correction is explained.

The considered weak decays are :

\[\Xi^{-}\rightarrow\Lambda+\pi^{-}(b.r.=0.999) \tag{4.10}\]

\[\overline{\Xi}^{+}\rightarrow\overline{\Lambda}+\pi^{+}(b.r.=0.999) \tag{4.11}\]

There is also a contribution of \(\Sigma^{0}\) in the inclusive \(\Lambda\) yield, however since this is a strong decay, and thus occurs at the primary vertex, no attempt to identify this contribution is made. Generally, \(\Lambda\) yields are understood to

