#### Cross-checks

Different cross-checks have been performed in order to exclude some common reasons for spurious signals and statistical fluctuations. The following checks have been done:

1. One potential hazard is a \(K^{-}/\pi^{-}\) mis-identification which could lead to a false reconstruction of the \(N^{*}\) resonance. In particular we checked that no \(\theta^{+}\) peak was visible when cutting on the invariant mass of this "false \(N^{*}\) ".
2. According to Dzierba et al [98] some experiments measuring inclusive signals were victims to spurious signal peaks due to \(p/\pi^{+}\) misidentification of a \(\Lambda\) decay. The \(\Lambda\) decay is then reconstructed as K\({}_{\rm s}^{0}\) and mixed with the proton daughter resulting in a sharp peak around the expected \(\theta^{+}\) mass. We have verified that there are no entries in the \(\Lambda\) invariant mass region that could be created by such a mis-identification.

